[b]📅   Nov. 10-19, 2025[/b]
•   [b]Project Deliverable:[/b] Laptop (HP Pavilion dv6-2102TX) repair and system upgrade.
•   [b]Configuration:[/b] Fixed with battery pack replacement. Extracted installed 64-bit Windows 7 Professional’s License key and included it in the deliverable via repair log. Upgraded to Windows 10 with Microsoft Office 2016. Advised to replace CMOS battery as system time was getting out of sync when not connected to the internet. Client was aunt’s friend.

[center]________________________________________________________________________________[/center]

[b]📅   Oct. 22-Nov. 6, 2025[/b]
•   [b]Project Deliverable:[/b] Laptop (Acer Aspire 4739) repair, bios bypass, and reformat/installation of WindowsOS.
•   [b]Configuration:[/b] Needed charging adapter cable replacement then battery pack replacement. BIOS Admin Password was present, used Windows 7’s vulnerability to install EasyBCD in order to be able to boot into the Windows Installer Pen Drive and install Windows 10. Because somehow I can't utilize a supposed a Bios Reset Pin-Jumping or even removing the CMOS Battery doesn't reset it. Later on, found the laptop’s original BIOS Firmware online and flashed/overwrote it to remove the BIOS Password. Client was aunt’s business acquaintance.
•   [b][url=www.facebook.com/share/v/1CUn23sHsU/]Reference[/url][/b]
