[b]📅   May, 2025[/b]
•   [b]Health Status:[/b] Radial Nerve Palsy on left arm.
•   [b]Description:[/b] Soon after the below entry(chronologically) I got Radial Nerve Palsy for another bizarre case of my body failing to protect itself which is rare unless intended because since a kid I was always moving and even inline skated, via sleeping on the arm. Like the Lasik after-surgery in the coming entries where my hand jerked to dislocate my left eye's healing 'flaps', this time it was my left arm to hand where I couldn't move my wrist to hand at all. It got better and able to move 100% again by the time I am writing this, though still feeling a little stiffness when I stretch up the fingers. There should be digital records in my messages with my mom on Facebook Messenger about it. Since we had it Electromyography-ed(EMg). During this time saw a video about it that said it would take about 6-9 Months to heal with theraphy. So I just switched from using Computer Keyboard to Gamepad/Controller for gaming as theraphy after my medicine for it ran out.

[center]________________________________________________________________________________[/center]

[b]📅   May 25, 2025[/b]
•   [b]Personal Endeavor:[/b] Investigating voting machine software versions using RegEx.
•   [b]Configuration:[/b] Just a personal curiosity-driven investigation after catching news online of a local lawyer publicly calling out that the voting machine software versions in the official records served to the public via the government website and what’s actually showing up on people’s ballots/receipts are not the same. Used RegEx a few times since College for “email format validation” and others. Used it again in this case to make the file hash records' format which was in PDF, match each other for easy comparison. After the election, it was reported anyway that the general populace was content with the results, so public acceptance is fine then, meaning they deem it consistent with cross-checking their fellow countrymen.
•   [b]References:[/b]
•   [url=github.com/AVSGamer/May_2025_General_Elections_ACM_File_Hashes_Between_Versions/tree/main]GitHub Repository with the Related Files[/url]
•   [url=www.youtube.com/watch?v=X60bojJXn4s]Video Re-upload[/url]

