[b]📅   Mar. 9, 2025[/b]
•   [b]After winning as 3rd Placer in the 14-Day Web3 Game Jam/Hackathon:[/b] Decided to take a break from Web3 gaming.
•   Decided to take a break from videogames that has cryptocurrencies and YGG which is a Filipino Developer Co-founded Legal Entity of multiple guilds, whose vision is to help gamers learn and earn while playing or doing tasks in the game using the verification of the blockchain integrated into the partnered games. As of writing this I am still in those communities albeit only checking in from time to time if there’s something I wanted to check like some news or updates about the games I spent a good amount of time, effort and involvement in. I mostly expect people to send me a direct private message if I am even needed. This is after getting the prize money from the tournament earlier and to go back to traditional Web2 or games that doesn’t have cryptocurrency for the reason of how blockchain technology is still new and top traditional game producer companies are skeptical of its scalability, I guess. Hence the design of a lot of the Web3 Games at the time wasn’t up to par with the types of games I used to play, which a lot of are not Free-to-Play games or High-Grossing Gacha/Games. The earning aspect for regular gamers is amazing, that’s not allowed on most Web2 games and treated as breaking the TOS. For about 3 years I was doing this Play-to-Earn and here is the link to my YGG Profile where all my NFTs indicating I have completed the GAP Tasks and claimed the corresponding monetary/crypto reward. This is not the same as online gambling/casino games though I had a share of experience working as OJT for one aspiring to host those. The achievements are supposedly NFTs tied to my YGG account. By that I mean some of them are still not visible in OpenSea website where you can see NFTs and Cryptocurrencies in a person’s crypto wallet:
