[b]📅   Sep. 26, 2024[/b]
•   [b]Still an intern until now unfortunately been doing other things:[/b] Online Game Server programmer internship for Shin Megami Tensei: Imagine Online preservation server.
•   [b]Motives:[/b] This game used to be officially hosted and published by ATLUS in Japan and by Playpark in Global or SEA Server; It’s an MMORPG game that made a lasting impact on my life. I was in homeschooling for 4th Year of my High-School at that time. I played this game a lot back then and where I met online, Aki who was using the Gamer Handle 'Syusuke' back then, a Japanese guy working in the field of IT, he was around 20 years old back then from what I can remember him telling me through the in-game chat system and eventually became part of my Facebook Friends to this day. Now there are some of us who miss this game and want to preserve it so they took it upon themselves to re-host the game after the official servers went down. New Moon is the name of the new server that I became an intern for and I was part of 1 patch. I chose a task to get me started that was supposedly relatively easy to help me get accustomed to what actual codebase did the developers that ATLUS hired for this game. The team was kind to show me the ropes in finding which files to look in then I studied the code structure to find what I needed to change. The task was to change some items’ (about 7~ items) inventory stack sizes and their category to be put in the other in-game storage/bank like the other items. I don't think it's a secret since it should be obvious that someone did release the encrypted files' decrypter and re-encrypter so we use those for the changes. This is a Non-Profit game server since the original game files' licenses are still owned by the original makers. Main reason why I couldn't get into it much, but hoping to get back to it eventually, probably soon after my plans this website is mostly done since I can feel my interest in gaming waning recently.
•   [b][url=54.39.131.171:3000/home]Game's Website[/url][/b]

